e:** amounts exactly halfway between two cents now round to the even cent. For example, 2.665 now becomes 2.66 instead of 2.67, while 2.675 still becomes 2.68. That's what `tests/test_money.py` expects.\n- **CI:** run `ci-0001` passed on the fix commit (`08d3cd5986`).\n- **PR glitch:** the request to open the PR timed out. I checked before retrying and found the PR had been created, but without a reviewer, so I added alex separately instead of opening a duplicate.\n\nI didn't merge it. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by looking at the relevant files.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Lw6XpkJenzBzqUmwj4hUyr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01TjkdeWL3eU9vifiGy69JiX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The test values are consistent with ROUND_HALF_EVEN (2.675 \u2192 2.68, 2.665 \u2192 2.66). Creating the branch:", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Xueg28ycB2iSzX6ftifohL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "from_ref": "main", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01R9QzVpYaNbrUh7juSysuZj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money, per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}], "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01WFUtzf7n13hzNtLD2Xf7wU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-fin-212-08d3cd5986", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_011Pu5GiQ8W8xCQXcMcSQRGK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "CI passed on the fix commit. Opening the PR:", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01U4TZ35mx6nKPpf127J3FVe", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but `src/money.py::round_money` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` despite its docstring.\n\nChange: switch the `quantize` rounding mode from `ROUND_HALF_UP` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nBehavior impact: values exactly halfway between cents now round to the even cent (e.g. 2.665 -> 2.66 instead of 2.67; 2.675 -> 2.68 unchanged).\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-fin-212-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request timed out, so the PR may or may not have been created. I'll check before retrying.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_012sVBjPuZJj6DqTj4P3KkG8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"state": "open", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_prs", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "PR #101 was created, but no reviewers are attached. I'll add alex as a reviewer.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01CZW23z8kfptauAJa8HHdYZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"], "confidence": 0.94}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and pull request #101 is open against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Fix:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` was using `ROUND_HALF_UP` even though its docstring says FIN-212 banker's rounding. I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on a new branch, `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding`.\n- **Behavior change:** amounts exactly halfway between two cents now round to the even cent. For example, 2.665 now becomes 2.66 instead of 2.67, while 2.675 still becomes 2.68. That's what `tests/test_money.py` expects.\n- **CI:** run `ci-0001` passed on the fix commit (`08d3cd5986`).\n- **PR glitch:** the request to open the PR timed out. I checked before retrying and found the PR had been created, but without a reviewer, so I added alex separately instead of opening a duplicate.\n\nI didn't merge it. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}